{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188451": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Position in Operations Management and Data Analytics 2027-2028",
      "description": "Posted: Jun 22, 2026 Deadline: Nov 30, 2026 Department: IE University: Business School Location: Madrid The Operations & Business Analytics Department at IE University´s Business School invites applications for multiple faculty positions in Operations Management and Data Analytics, with appointments beginning in September 2027. We welcome applications from candidates at different career stages. Outstanding candidates may be considered for appointment at the Assistant Professor (tenure-track), Associate Professor, or Full Professor level, depending on qualifications, experience, and scholarly achievements. We seek scholars broadly interested in empirical research on operations management, supply chain management, service operations, decision making, and data analytics. We particularly welcome candidates whose methodological orientation includes non-experimental approaches (e.g., econometric modeling, analytics, machine learning, or optimization) and/or experimental methods (e.g., field or laboratory experiments). The department values diverse research approaches and encourages applications from candidates with backgrounds in operations management, management science, decision sciences, business analytics, data science, or related disciplines. Successful candidates will be expected to: Conduct high-quality research publishable in top-tier academic journals; Teach courses in operations management, supply chain management, business analytics, data analytics, and related areas at the undergraduate, graduate, and/or executive levels; Contribute to the intellectual life and strategic development of the department and IE University; and Provide academic leadership commensurate with their rank and experience. Additional Information English is the main language of instruction and institutional communications. Spanish is not required, nor expected. IE University offers a highly international and entrepreneurial academic environment. Salary is competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. About IE University IE University, which grew out of IE Business School, has taken a leading position in Europe among institutions of higher education for its excellence in innovation and learning technologies. In addition to the Business School , IE hosts Schools in Law , Politics, Economics and Global Affairs, Architecture and Design , Humanities , and Science & Technology . IE’s programs are highly ranked and recognized in the international press. IE has an internationally and culturally highly diverse faculty. IE University has campuses in Madrid and Segovia, Spain. Madrid is a vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of 5 million that offers an enormous range of professional and leisure opportunities. Segovia is a beautiful World-Heritage city that offers the pleasures of a small city environment, the possibility of many outdoor activities, and easy access (30 minutes by bullet train) to the heart of bustling Madrid. Please visit: IE University to learn more. A Ph.D. (or expected completion by the appointment date for junior candidates) in Operations Management, Management Science, Decision Sciences, Data or Business Analytics, or a related field from an internationally recognized institution. For senior appointments, an established record of impactful research, teaching excellence, and academic leadership consistent with rank. Application Materials Cover letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) Research statement Teaching statement Copies of recent publications or working papers Evidence of teaching excellence (e.g., teaching evaluations) Contact information for three references Applications received by November 30, 2026 will receive full consideration and should be submitted via Interfolio at: https://apply.interfolio.com/188451 For inquiries regarding th e position, please contact Prof. Daniel Corsten at Daniel.Corsten@ie.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195131": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Public Law 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: Law School Location: Madrid & Segovia, Spain IE University invites applicationsinvites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in the Department of Public Law of IE Law School. The appointment will begin on September 1, 2027. The Department of Public Law of IE Law School brings together scholars whose research and teaching span a wide range of fields, including public international law, European Union law, constitutional law, human rights, administrative law and regulation, criminal law and procedure, and tax law. We seek candidates with an original and relevant research agenda and the potential to build a strong record of high-impact publications. Consistent with the school’s global orientation, we are interested in scholarship that speaks to audiences across jurisdictions and contributes to broader debates about law, institutions, societal challenges, and public policy. We welcome methodological diversity, including comparative, transnational, empirical, socio-legal, economic, political economy and other interdisciplinary approaches, alongside doctrinal and theoretical work. We welcome applications from candidates across all areas of public law, although subject areas of particular interest include climate, environmental and energy law; international economic and trade law; human rights; and tax law. English is our working language and the primary language of instruction. Most courses are taught from a transnational or comparative perspective. Knowledge of Spanish or Spanish law is therefore not required. Departmental Fit We are simultaneously advertising several openings in the Departments of Public and Private Law. We recognize that many areas of legal scholarship cross traditional disciplinary boundaries. However, we ask candidates to apply to a single position, choosing the one they believe best fits their research and teaching profile. This choice will not prevent an application from being considered for a different position if we believe there may be a better fit. What we offer Competitive salary, in line with top-ranked European academic institutions. Generous seed fund to cover conference, travel, equipment and relocation costs. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme, plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Professional and stimulating working environment in the context of a diverse, innovative and multidisciplinary scholarly community, with English as the main working language. Access to the opportunities and resources of CIVICA – The European University of Social Sciences , the Law Schools Global League , the European Law Faculties Association , and the Center for Transnational Legal Studies . Inspiring campus life in Madrid (a vibrant, cosmopolitan city of over five million) and Segovia (a UNESCO World Heritage city with fast access to Madrid). Candidates should have a PhD in Law or JSD/SJD (or demonstrate clear evidence that their PhD or JSD/SJD will be completed by July 2027). To be considered, please create your dossier and apply via Interfolio no later than November 10th via Interfolio at: https://apply.interfolio.com/195131 Early applications are encouraged. Submit the following materials: Cover letter outlining your research agenda Curriculum vitae, including a full list of publications One representative article or sample research paper Contact information for two potential referees, who will only be contacted, if needed, after prior notice to the candidate Longlisted candidates will be invited to a video interview. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to present a recent publication or a work-in-progress on campus. Pre-submission inquiries about the positions may be addressed to Sara Junquera ( sara.junquera@ie.edu ), Executive Director of Faculty and Accreditations at IE Law School."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195132": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Private Law 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: Law School Location: Madrid & Segovia, Spain IE University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in the Department of Private Law of IE Law School. The appointment will begin on September 1, 2027. The Department of Private Law of IE Law School brings together scholars whose research and teaching span a wide range of fields, including contract law, tort law, property law, family law, IP law, civil procedure and arbitration, private international law, private law theory, commercial and business law, labour law, and competition law. We seek candidates with an original and relevant research agenda and the potential to build a strong record of high-impact publications. Consistent with the school’s global orientation, we are interested in scholarship that speaks to audiences across jurisdictions and contributes to broader debates about law, institutions, societal challenges, and public policy. We welcome methodological diversity, including comparative, transnational, empirical, socio-legal, economic, political economy and other interdisciplinary approaches, alongside doctrinal and theoretical work. We welcome applications from candidates across all areas of private law, although subject areas of particular interest include corporate law, financial law; intellectual property law; and core private law (contracts, property, and torts). English is our working language and the primary language of instruction. Most courses are taught from a transnational or comparative perspective. Knowledge of Spanish or Spanish law is therefore not required. Departmental Fit We are simultaneously advertising several openings in the Departments of Public and Private Law. We recognize that many areas of legal scholarship cross traditional disciplinary boundaries. However, we ask candidates to apply to a single position, choosing the one they believe best fits their research and teaching profile. This choice will not prevent an application from being considered for a different position if we believe there may be a better fit. What we offer Competitive salary, in line with top-ranked European academic institutions. Generous seed fund to cover conference, travel, equipment and relocation costs. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme, plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Professional and stimulating working environment in the context of a diverse, innovative and multidisciplinary scholarly community, with English as the main working language. Access to the opportunities and resources of CIVICA – The European University of Social Sciences , the Law Schools Global League , the European Law Faculties Association , and the Center for Transnational Legal Studies . Inspiring campus life in Madrid (a vibrant, cosmopolitan city of over five million) and Segovia (a UNESCO World Heritage city with fast access to Madrid). Candidates should have a PhD in Law or JSD/SJD (or demonstrate clear evidence that their PhD or JSD/SJD will be completed by July 2027). To be considered, please create your dossier and apply via Interfolio no later than November 10th at: https://apply.interfolio.com/195132 Early applications are encouraged. Submit the following materials: Cover letter outlining your research agenda Curriculum vitae, including a full list of publications One representative article or sample research paper Contact information for two potential referees, who will only be contacted, if needed, after prior notice to the candidate Longlisted candidates will be invited to an online interview. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to campus to present a recent publication or work in progress and meet with members of the faculty. Inquiries about the position may be addressed to Sara Junquera ( sara.junquera@ie.edu ), Executive Director of Faculty and Accreditations at IE Law School."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195192": {
      "title": "Professor of Law (Tenured/Senior Appointment) - 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: Law School Location: Madrid & Segovia, Spain IE University invites applications for a senior appointment in Law beginning September 2027. IE Law School is investing strategically in the growth and development of its research faculty, with the ambition of becoming a leading European hub for legal scholarship. We seek an internationally recognized scholar with a sustained record of publications in leading journals and a clear trajectory of high-impact research in law. Consistent with the school’s global orientation, we are interested in scholarship that speaks to audiences across jurisdictions and contributes to broader debates about law, institutions, societal challenges, and public policy. We welcome methodological diversity, including comparative, transnational, empirical, socio-legal, economic, political economy and other interdisciplinary approaches, alongside doctrinal and theoretical work. In evaluating candidates, particular attention will be given to the scholarly impact and visibility of their research, including the quality and consistency of publications in leading journals, citation impact, engagement with the academic community through editorial and other academic leadership roles, success in attracting competitive international research funding, experience in doctoral supervision, and evidence of active research momentum. Consideration will also be given to evidence of research impact beyond academia, including engagement with courts, public authorities, international institutions, the legal profession and public policy. English is the working language and the main language of instruction. Most courses are taught from a transnational or comparative perspective. Knowledge of Spanish or Spanish law is therefore not required. What we offer Competitive salary, in line with top-ranked European academic institutions. Generous seed fund to cover conference, travel, equipment and relocation costs. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme, plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Professional and stimulating working environment in the context of a diverse, innovative and multidisciplinary scholarly community, with English as the main working language. Access to the opportunities and resources of CIVICA – The European University of Social Sciences , the Law Schools Global League , the European Law Faculties Association , and the Center for Transnational Legal Studies . Inspiring campus life in Madrid (a vibrant, cosmopolitan city of over five million) and Segovia (a UNESCO World Heritage city with fast access to Madrid). Candidates should demonstrate both a record of significant scholarly achievement and the capacity to contribute to the further development of IE Law School’s research community over the medium to long term. To be considered, please create your dossier and apply via Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/195192 Applications should include: A Cover letter. A Curriculum vitae, including a full list of publications Contact information for two potential referees, who will only be contacted, if needed, after prior notice to the candidate Applications received before November 10, 2026 , will receive full consideration . Review will continue until the position is filled. Informal enquiries are welcome and may be made in strict confidence to Fernando Pastor, Vice-Dean of Faculty and Research at IE Law School: fernando.pastor@ie.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193485": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Faculty and Research - IE School of Architecture and Design",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Architecture and Design Location: Madrid and Segovia IE University invites applications for the position of Associate Dean for Faculty and Research in the IE School of Architecture and Design. Reporting jointly to the Dean of the School of Architecture and Design and the IE University Vice Rector for Faculty and Research, the Associate Dean will provide academic leadership for the School's research strategy and faculty development. The Associate Dean will work closely with the Dean and the Vice Rector for Faculty and Research to: Develop and implement the School's research strategy. Mentor faculty in developing research agendas, publication strategies, and competitive funding applications. Advise faculty as they prepare for promotion and tenure processes. Foster interdisciplinary collaboration across the School and the wider University. Identify opportunities for external research funding, particularly through European and international programs. Represent the School on University-wide research committees and advocate for appropriate approaches to evaluating research in architecture and design. Contribute to the recruitment, mentoring, and long-term development of the School's faculty. The principal measure of success in this role will be the success of the School's faculty: supporting colleagues in building stronger research portfolios, securing competitive funding, and increasing the quality and impact of their scholarly and creative work. About the School IE School of Architecture and Design is an international, interdisciplinary school joining architecture, design, fashion, and real estate development within a single academic community. Our academic portfolio includes architecture, interior design, product design, strategic design, graphic design, immersive media, fashion design, business for architecture and design, and real estate development. We regard architecture and design as research disciplines as well as domains of professional practice. Our faculty conduct research through scholarly publications, funded projects, practice-based research, exhibitions, and collaborations with industry, public institutions, and communities. Across these activities, the School focuses on questions of material innovation, social impact through design, sustainable cities, entrepreneurship in creative fields, and authorship and identity. The successful candidate will be an internationally respected scholar with substantial academic leadership experience and a demonstrated commitment to faculty development. Applicants should have: A PhD in Architecture, Design, Engineering, Design History, Urbanism, or a closely related discipline. Appointment at the rank of Associate Professor (with tenure) or Full Professor , or equivalent. A strong record of research and scholarly publication. A sustained record of securing competitive external research funding and participating in major collaborative research initiatives. Experience mentoring faculty and supporting academic career development. Experience leading research centers, laboratories, institutes, or comparable academic initiatives. Experience participating in promotion and tenure processes, research evaluation, or institutional research governance. The School is particularly interested in candidates with a track record of transdisciplinary work in architecture and design. Experience with European research programs, including Horizon Europe, ERC, Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions, UKRI, or comparable international funding frameworks, is highly desirable. As an international university with over 100 nationalities present on campus, our working language is English. Knowledge of Spanish is not required. Please include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae A statement (2–3 pages) describing the candidate's approach to research leadership and faculty development A portfolio of the candidate’s most relevant publications and/or other research contributions Contact information for three references For consideration, create your dossier and apply at via Interfolio no later than 30 November 2026 at: https://apply.interfolio.com/193485"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182994": {
      "title": "Professor of Macroeconomics (Tenured/Senior Appointment) 2026",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Politics, Economics and Global Affairs Location: Madrid & Segovia, Spain IE University’s School of Politics, Economics & Global Affairs (IE-SPEGA) invites applications for a senior appointment in Macroeconomics beginning September 2026. IE-SPEGA is investing strategically in the rapid development of a research-intensive Economics Department, with the ambition of becoming a leading European hub for economic scholarship. We seek an internationally recognized scholar with a sustained record of publications in top-tier journals and a clear trajectory of high-impact research in macroeconomics (including monetary economics, international macroeconomics, macro-finance, business cycles, or growth). In evaluating candidates, particular attention will be given to the scholarly impact and visibility of their research, including the quality and consistency of publications in leading journals, citation influence, engagement with the academic community through editorial roles, and evidence of active research momentum, alongside a demonstrated capacity to contribute meaningfully to the department’s development over the medium to long term. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in shaping the department’s intellectual direction and strengthening its global research profile. We welcome candidates whose work combines theoretical depth, empirical rigor, and relevance to major global economic challenges. IE University offers competitive compensation, research support, and a highly international academic environment. English is the working language. Review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted directly. We seek an internationally recognized scholar with a sustained record of publications in top-tier journals and a clear trajectory of high-impact research in macroeconomics (including monetary economics, international macroeconomics, macro-finance, business cycles, or growth). Applications should include a CV, including  ORCID iD,  Scopus Author ID, at least two references, and selected publications. Review begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Please create your dossier at Interfolio and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/182994"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189255": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Accounting & Management Control 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: Business School: Accounting & Management Control Location: Madrid The Accounting and Management Control Department of IE University is seeking candidates in all areas of accounting for up to two tenure-track Assistant professorships beginning September 2027 . The Accounting and Management Control Department is part of a university research cluster that combines advanced empirical methods with rigorous theoretical models to study the policies and mechanisms shaping markets and society. Institutions, firms, and markets play a critical role in resource allocation and the functioning of modern economies. This cluster examines these dynamics to generate evidence-based insights that support smarter policy design and enrich public debate. The Department’s research interests are diverse covering financial reporting, management control systems, auditing, taxation, accounting history, accounting for non-profit organizations and sustainability reporting. The research methodologies used are also diverse, embracing quantitative and qualitative research. Although we welcome candidates working in any accounting-related area, for the near future we are particularly interested in the following two topics: Accounting and Technology and ESG reporting . Our faculty have published in top academic journals including the Accounting Review, Accounting Organizations and Society, Contemporary Accounting Research, the European Accounting Review, Journal of Business Finance and Accounting, Journal of Accounting and Public Policy, Auditing: A Journal of Practice and Theory, among others. They have won prestigious research grants awarded by national and international bodies. In addition, our faculty includes current or former Editors of the European Accounting Review and the Journal of Accounting and Public Policy, and a former president of the European Accounting Association. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. The successful candidate will be expected to publish in top-tier peer-reviewed journals and to become an excellent instructor in our programs. By the starting date, applicants should have a PhD degree in accounting, or in any other subject (e.g. Finance, Economics and Sociology) but with a clear focus on accounting. The degree should be granted by an internationally recognized school. To apply, please submit your dossier at Interfolio by November 15th, 2026 at: https://apply.interfolio.com/189255 Applications should include a cover letter, a CV, a job market paper, three confidential letters of recommendation, and evidence of teaching excellence if available (e.g. teaching evaluations). Participation in the Talent Workshop organized by the European Accounting Association (Madrid, 6-7 November 2026), is strongly encouraged. Candidates planning to attend the Talent Workshop do not need to submit their applications at Interfolio. The will have to submit their application package through the Talent Workshop website https://eaa-jobmarket.ie.edu/"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194685": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Economics 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Politics, Economics and Global Affairs: Economics Location: Madrid IE University is looking for applicants in macroeconomics to fill three tenure-track positions as Assistant or Associate Professor in the Department of Economics, starting September 2027. Position duties include publishing in leading economic journals, teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels, and contributing to the intellectual life of the School. We are looking for candidates in Macroeconomics , Monetary Economics , or Time-series Econometrics . Candidates are offered a competitive remuneration package, a dynamic research environment, and a cosmopolitan workplace in the heart of Madrid. English is the working language, and our faculty and students are highly diverse and international. Knowledge of Spanish is not required. Applicants should have completed or be close to completing a Ph.D. in Economics, Finance, or a related field from an internationally recognized institution by July 2027. Ph.D. in Economics, Finance, or a related field by July 2027. Interested applicants, please create your dossier and apply through Interfolio by November 15 , 2026 11:59 PM Eastern Time https://apply.interfolio.com/194685 Applications should include: A Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Job Market Paper Three Confidential letters of recommendation For queries about the application process, contact Sara.Flores@ie.edu For help with your dossier please go to Interfolio Help https://product-help.interfolio.com/en_US/dossier"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189894": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Finance 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: Business School: Finance Location: Madrid The Finance Department of IE University is seeking candidates in all areas of Finance for a tenure-track Assistant Professorship beginning September 2027. The Finance Department combines advanced empirical methods with rigorous theoretical models to study the policies and mechanisms shaping markets and society. Institutions, firms, and markets play a critical role in resource allocation and the functioning of modern economies. The Department’s research focuses on financial and real estate markets, corporate finance, managerial incentive structures, macro-finance interactions, and sustainable finance. We particularly welcome applicants whose research aligns with these areas and who employ cutting-edge AI tools in their work. The successful candidate will be expected to publish in top-tier peer-reviewed journals and to become an excellent teacher in our programs. By the starting date, applicants should have a PhD degree in Finance or Economics (with strong research credentials in Finance) from an internationally recognized school. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. ABOUT THE ORGANIZATION: IE University, which grew out of IE Business School, has taken a leading position in Europe among institutions of higher education for its excellence in innovation and learning technologies as well as a focus in sustainability. IE’s programs are highly ranked. IE’s diverse faculty comes from around the world, and is encouraged to develop excellence in research, teaching, and leadership within their areas of expertise. The Finance Group offers courses at the undergraduate, graduate, executive and Ph.D. levels. The Group is very collegial and has a strong focus on high-quality teaching and academic research. To learn more, visit IE Business School By the starting date, applicants should have a PhD in Finance or Economics (with strong research credentials in Finance) from an internationally recognized school. To apply, please create your dossier at Interfolio by November 15, 2026 at: https://apply.interfolio.com/189894 Applications should include a cover letter, a CV, a job market paper, three confidential letters of recommendation, and evidence of teaching excellence if available (e.g. teaching evaluations)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195023": {
      "title": "Research Associate Economics and Business",
      "description": "Department: IE University: Business School: Finance Location: Madrid IE University´s Business School seeks applicants for a Research Associate in Economics and Business to collaborate in INTEGRED (DOI: 10.3030/101289618) ), a Horizon Europe project that explores an Integrative Approach to the Production, Use and Governance of Evidence in European Education, under the supervision of Dr. Antonio Roldán. The 18-month temporary project-based contract includes a 40.000 gross annual salary and a dedication of 40 hrs/week in Madrid, with the possibility of a percentage of hybrid work. Tasks description: Contribute to the design, planning and implementation of RCTs in education. Design data-collection processes and build the databases required for the different experiments. Clean, manage and analyze quantitative data using appropriate statistical and econometric methods. Assist in the design of surveys and other research instruments. Support field implementation and coordinate with participating institutions, research partners and implementation teams. Coordinate multidisciplinary and international teams involved in the project. Contribute to the operational, administrative and communication activities of the Horizon Europe project, with support from IE University’s administrative staff. Help prepare research reports, presentations and academic outputs. Support the preparation and coordination of technical and financial reports with the Research Office for submission to the Project Coordinator Opportunity to co-author academic publications based on susbtantive contributuins to the research, in line with project norms Essential Qualifications: Strong quantitative and data-analysis skills. Proficiency in at least one relevant statistical programming language, such as Stata, R or Python and fluent use of AI tools. Previous experience in designing or implementing RCTs. Ability to manage, clean and document complex datasets rigorously. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within large and international teams. Advanced Master’s degree or PhD—or expected completion—in economics, public policy or a related discipline. Desirable Qualifications: Experience designing surveys and managing field-data collection. Previous experience designing, implementing or analyzing randomized controlled trials or other field experiments. Experience coordinating with schools, public administrations, NGOs or other implementation partners. Excellent organizational skills and the capacity to manage several workstreams simultaneously. Research expertise or substantive knowledge in the economics of education, education policy or labor economics. Familiarity with reproducible research practices, pre-analysis plans and research documentation. Experience in the coordination of project-related technical and financial reporting, preferably in the context of Horizon Europe Create your dossier and apply by October 23rd at Interfolio https://apply.interfolio.com/195023 Applications should include: CV Cover Letter (optional) Contact References (optional) For help with your private and personal dossier go to: https://product-help.interfolio.com/en_US/dossier help@interfolio.com For questions about the application reach out to anna.doherty@ie.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190002": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty positions in Computer Science: Networks and Complex Systems 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia I E University´s School of Science and Technology invites qualified applicants for full-time, tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Science, beginning September 2027 in Madrid. To guarantee full consideration for a position, applications must be completed by October 31st, 2026. Applicants for this position should demonstrate a strong research record in core areas of networks and complex systems, including: graph learning, graph neural networks, network representation learning, temporal and dynamic graphs, network optimization, complex systems modeling, network science, community detection, diffusion processes, graph signal processing, knowledge graphs, multi-layer networks, hypergraphs, causal networks, recommendation algorithms. These fundamental methods should be demonstrated through applications in domains such as: systems biology, neuroscience, epidemiology, social networks, anomaly detection, cybersecurity, multi-agent systems, swarm robotics, transportation networks, communication networks, power grids, infrastructure planning, supply chains, financial networks, or smart cities. For more details on the research conducted at the School, see the webpages of its labs: Intelligent Systems , Datalab , EnvironmentalTech , and the Impact Xcelerator . We offer: A friendly, professional, and stimulating international working environment with English as our working language. A competitive salary in line with top ranked European academic institutions. A seed research fund to cover conference, travel, equipment or relocation costs. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Newly incoming high-qualified workers in Spain are entitled to a considerable income tax reduction. Diversity in an open-minded, inclusive and family-friendly environment. Inspiring campus life on a conveniently located, architecturally unique campus in the heart of Madrid and Segovia. About IE University and the School of Science and Technology IE University is an internationally recognized institution originally founded as a business school. We consider ourselves the most international institution of higher education with approximately 85% of our students coming from outside Spain and typically over 120 countries represented on campus. Our Madrid postgraduate campus is situated in the financial district of this vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of over 5 million people. In 2021 we opened the IE Tower –standing as one of the 5 towers in the business district of Madrid with a 6000-student capacity. The School of Science and Technology prepares students with industry relevant skills in the context of STEM and related educational programs. The school offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Applied Mathematics and Data analytics. Our Master’s in Business analytics and Big Data had our university ranked No. 7 globally for Master's in Business Analytics. The school boasts a diverse and international faculty of engineers, computer scientists, applied mathematicians, and experts in AI, cybersecurity, NLP and information technologies. The IE Impact Xcelerator offers new faculty the opportunity to participate in applied research labs in collaboration with research groups and companies in fields like healthcare, environmental science, finance, and cybersecurity, profiting from the rich network of IE Business School. PhD in computer science, computer engineering, or a closely related discipline. Excellence in research evidenced primarily by sustained contributions and publications in top-ranked and field relevant journals. Independence and ability to lead research projects in your field. New faculty is expected to submit research proposals to attract funds in competitive calls. Ability to participate in applied research and knowledge transfer in interdisciplinary teams at the interface between technical and application-oriented domains. Strong commitment to teaching curricula in and around computer science. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. Create your dossier at Interfolio by October 31st and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/190002 Please include a CV and cover letter, research and teaching statements, and three reference contacts. You may also add teaching evaluations and sample course syllabi to your dossier. For questions about your dossier go to: Interfolio Dossier Help"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190036": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty positions in Computer Science: Sustainable and Emerging Computing 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia I E University´s School of Science and Technology invites qualified applicants for full-time, tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Science, beginning September 2027 in Madrid. To guarantee full consideration for a position, applications must be completed by October 31st, 2026. Applicants for this position should demonstrate a strong research record in core areas of sustainable and emerging computing, including: energy-efficient machine learning, carbon-aware scheduling, energy-aware resource allocation, sustainable cloud computing, energy-efficient distributed systems, compiler and runtime optimization, hardware–software co-design, approximate computing, low-power computing, workload optimization, or lifecycle assessment of computing systems. These fundamental methods should be demonstrated through applications in domains such as: high-performance computing, cloud and edge computing, sustainable data centers, AI model training and inference, the Internet of Things (IoT), mobile and embedded systems, smart grids, renewable energy integration, industrial computing, digital twins, scientific computing, telecommunications, or carbon accounting. For more details on the research conducted at the School, see the webpages of its labs: Intelligent Systems , Datalab , EnvironmentalTech , and the Impact Xcelerator . We offer: A friendly, professional, and stimulating international working environment with English as our working language. A competitive salary in line with top ranked European academic institutions. A seed research fund to cover conference, travel, equipment or relocation costs. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Newly incoming high-qualified workers in Spain are entitled to a considerable income tax reduction. Diversity in an open-minded, inclusive and family-friendly environment. Inspiring campus life on a conveniently located, architecturally unique campus in the heart of Madrid and Segovia. About IE University and the School of Science and Technology IE University is an internationally recognized institution originally founded as a business school. We consider ourselves the most international institution of higher education with approximately 85% of our students coming from outside Spain and typically over 120 countries represented on campus. Our Madrid postgraduate campus is situated in the financial district of this vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of over 5 million people. In 2021 we opened the IE Tower –standing as one of the 5 towers in the business district of Madrid with a 6000-student capacity. The School of Science and Technology prepares students with industry relevant skills in the context of STEM and related educational programs. The school offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Applied Mathematics and Data analytics. Our Master’s in Business analytics and Big Data had our university ranked No. 7 globally for Master's in Business Analytics. The school boasts a diverse and international faculty of engineers, computer scientists, applied mathematicians, and experts in AI, cybersecurity, NLP and information technologies. The IE Impact Xcelerator offers new faculty the opportunity to participate in applied research labs in collaboration with research groups and companies in fields like healthcare, environmental science, finance, and cybersecurity, profiting from the rich network of IE Business School. PhD in computer science, computer engineering, or a closely related discipline. Excellence in research evidenced primarily by sustained contributions and publications in top-ranked and field relevant journals. Independence and ability to lead research projects in your field. New faculty is expected to submit research proposals to attract funds in competitive calls. Ability to participate in applied research and knowledge transfer in interdisciplinary teams at the interface between technical and application-oriented domains. Strong commitment to teaching curricula in and around computer science. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. Create your dossier at Interfolio by October 31st and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/190036 Please include a CV and cover letter, research and teaching statements, and three reference contacts. You may also add teaching evaluations and sample course syllabi to your dossier. For questions about your dossier go to: Interfolio Dossier Help"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190038": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty positions in Computer Science: Cybersecurity, Privacy and AI Safety 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia I E University´s School of Science and Technology invites qualified applicants for full-time, tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Science, beginning September 2027 in Madrid. To guarantee full consideration for a position, applications must be completed by October 31st, 2026. Applicants for this position should demonstrate a strong research record in core areas such as: adversarial machine learning, AI robustness, verification and formal methods, cryptography, fraud detection, intrusion detection, AI alignment, calibration, conformal prediction, uncertainty quantification, AI interpretability and explainability, or risk-aware decision making. These fundamental methods should be demonstrated through applications in domains such as: cybersecurity, healthcare, robotics, autonomous vehicles, industrial automation, critical infrastructure, energy systems, finance, scientific AI, public sector AI, or human-AI collaboration. For more details on the research conducted at the School, see the webpages of its labs: Intelligent Systems , Datalab , EnvironmentalTech , and the Impact Xcelerator . We offer: A friendly, professional, and stimulating international working environment with English as our working language. A competitive salary in line with top ranked European academic institutions. A seed research fund to cover conference, travel, equipment or relocation costs. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Newly incoming high-qualified workers in Spain are entitled to a considerable income tax reduction. Diversity in an open-minded, inclusive and family-friendly environment. Inspiring campus life on a conveniently located, architecturally unique campus in the heart of Madrid and Segovia. About IE University and the School of Science and Technology IE University is an internationally recognized institution originally founded as a business school. We consider ourselves the most international institution of higher education with approximately 85% of our students coming from outside Spain and typically over 120 countries represented on campus. Our Madrid postgraduate campus is situated in the financial district of this vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of over 5 million people. In 2021 we opened the IE Tower –standing as one of the 5 towers in the business district of Madrid with a 6000-student capacity. The School of Science and Technology prepares students with industry relevant skills in the context of STEM and related educational programs. The school offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Applied Mathematics and Data analytics. Our Master’s in Business analytics and Big Data had our university ranked No. 7 globally for Master's in Business Analytics. The school boasts a diverse and international faculty of engineers, computer scientists, applied mathematicians, and experts in AI, cybersecurity, NLP and information technologies. The IE Impact Xcelerator offers new faculty the opportunity to participate in applied research labs in collaboration with research groups and companies in fields like healthcare, environmental science, finance, and cybersecurity, profiting from the rich network of IE Business School. PhD in computer science, computer engineering, or a closely related discipline. Excellence in research evidenced primarily by sustained contributions and publications in top-ranked and field relevant journals. Independence and ability to lead research projects in your field. New faculty is expected to submit research proposals to attract funds in competitive calls. Ability to participate in applied research and knowledge transfer in interdisciplinary teams at the interface between technical and application-oriented domains. Strong commitment to teaching curricula in and around computer science. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. Create your dossier at Interfolio by October 31st and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/190038 Please include a CV and cover letter, research and teaching statements, and three reference contacts. You may also add teaching evaluations and sample course syllabi to your dossier. For questions about your dossier go to: Interfolio Dossier Help"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192572": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Mathematics for AI and Scientific Discovery 2027–2028",
      "description": "Posted: Aug 31, 2026 Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia IE University´s School of Science and Technology invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Mathematics for AI and Scientific Discovery . We seek outstanding candidates developing mathematical, statistical, and computational foundations for modern artificial intelligence, particularly researchers interested in using these methods to advance scientific discovery. This position targets researchers whose primary methodological contribution lies in artificial intelligence, machine learning, probabilistic modeling, or their mathematical foundations, rather than primarily in traditional numerical analysis or computational modeling. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in areas such as Mathematics for Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Optimization for AI, Probability and Statistics, Scientific Machine Learning, and AI for Science. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. Research Profile We are particularly interested in candidates working in one or more of the following areas: Mathematical foundations of AI: learning theory, approximation theory, high-dimensional probability, information theory, mathematical analysis of neural networks, representation learning, robustness, and interpretability. Probabilistic modeling and statistical AI: probabilistic machine learning, Bayesian methods, uncertainty quantification, stochastic modeling, and statistical learning. Optimization for AI: mathematical optimization for machine learning, large-scale and stochastic optimization, variational methods, and optimization of modern AI models. Scientific machine learning: physics-informed and physics-constrained machine learning, neural differential equations, operator learning, machine learning for dynamical systems, and hybrid mechanistic/data-driven models. Computational methods for scientific discovery: AI-assisted simulation, surrogate modeling, inverse learning problems, automated scientific discovery, generative approaches for science, and data-driven discovery of mathematical or physical structure. Research Environment: IE Research Datalab The successful candidate will have the opportunity to become an active member of the IE Research Datalab , an interdisciplinary research environment within the IE School of Science and Technology bringing together researchers across applied mathematics, statistics, optimization, data science, machine learning, and computational science. The Datalab combines fundamental methodological research with interdisciplinary and applied research, providing a natural environment for connecting mathematical and statistical methodology with modern artificial intelligence and scientific applications. Its research activities span areas including Data Science and Machine Learning, Applied Mathematics, Operations Research, Statistical Modelling, and Computational Biology. For this position, particularly relevant areas of interaction include machine learning, Bayesian statistics, probabilistic modeling, optimization, high-dimensional computational methods, and AI-driven scientific applications. The successful candidate will be encouraged to strengthen connections across these areas through an independent research program in mathematically grounded AI and scientific machine learning. Explore the IE Research Data Lab to know more about its research activities, projects, publications, and faculty. Impact Xcelerator Collaboration We particularly value candidates with the capacity to collaborate in applied research projects led by the IEX Labs at IE School of Science and Technology, especially in areas such as AI for Scientific Discovery , Health and MedTech, Advanced Simulation for Energy and Sustainability, Robotics and Autonomous Systems, Digital Twins, and Data-Driven Decision Making. The ability to build bridges between mathematical foundations, modern AI methodologies, and substantive scientific problems will be central to the role. K ey Responsibilities: Develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Mathematics for AI, Machine Learning, Optimization for AI, Probability and Statistics, Scientific Machine Learning, and AI for Science. Conduct internationally recognized research in mathematically grounded AI, machine learning, probabilistic modeling, scientific machine learning, or AI for scientific discovery. Pursue competitive external research funding. Supervise and mentor undergraduate, master’s, and PhD students. Build interdisciplinary collaborations connecting mathematics and AI with scientific and technological domains. Collaborate with researchers in mathematics, computer science, engineering, and the natural and life sciences, as well as with industry and external research partners. Contribute to curriculum development in mathematical AI, scientific machine learning, uncertainty quantification, and AI for Science. Participate in academic service and contribute to the strategic growth of the Department of Mathematics and the School of Science and Technology. We Offer: A competitive salary in line with top-ranked European academic institutions. A generous seed research fund to cover travel, equipment and relocation costs. State-of-the-art campus facilities and support to build your lab infrastructure. A professional and stimulating international working environment with English as the working language. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme, plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. An open, inclusive, and family-friendly academic environment. Inspiring campuses in the heart of Madrid and Segovia. About IE University and the School of Science and Technology IE University is an internationally recognized institution originally founded as a business school. We consider ourselves the most international institution of higher education with approximately 85% international students representing more than 120 countries. The School of Science and Technology offers undergraduate and graduate programs in Applied Mathematics, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, and related STEM disciplines, fostering excellence in research, innovation, and interdisciplinary education. The School is committed to advancing research at the intersection of mathematics, statistics, computation, and artificial intelligence, with particular emphasis on emerging approaches that combine mathematical foundations and AI to accelerate scientific discovery. PhD in Applied Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, Computational Science, Physics, Engineering  or relevant field by the appointment date, or a closely related area. Postdoctoral research experience is desirable but not required. Evidence of excellent research potential or achievement, including recent high-quality publications. Potential to attract competitive external funding. Commitment to excellent teaching, student supervision, and inclusive mentorship. Ability to contribute to interdisciplinary science and technology programs. Particular interest will be given to researchers developing methods with applications in areas such as physics, engineering, climate and environmental science, energy, materials science, life sciences, neuroscience, health, or other scientific domains. Faculty are expected to engage in high-quality research, pursue competitive external funding, supervise students, and contribute to curriculum development and university service. Create your dossier at Interfolio by October 31st and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/192572 Applications received before November 1st, 2026 will receive full consideration. The position will remain open until it is filled. Application Materials Cover letter. Curriculum vitae, including recent publications, funding record, teaching experience and supervision record. Research statement, including main achievements and future research plans for the next five years. Teaching statement. Evidence of teaching quality, if available. Up to three representative publications. Shortlisted candidates invited to an online interview may be asked to provide two to three confidential recommendation letters at a later stage. Pre-submission inquiries about the open positions may be addressed to Prof. Dae-Jin Lee Dae-Jin.Lee@ie.edu For questions about your dossier, please go to: Interfolio Dossier Help"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192573": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty positions in Applied Mathematics and Computational Modeling 2027-2028",
      "description": "Posted: Aug 31, 2026 Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia I E University´s School of Science and Technology invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Applied Mathematics and Computational Modeling. We seek outstanding candidates whose research is centered on the mathematical modeling, analysis, numerical solution, and simulation of physical, engineering, or complex systems. The position is particularly suited to researchers with a strong background in applied and computational mathematics who develop mathematical models and numerical methodologies for scientifically relevant problems. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in areas such as Numerical Methods, Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations, Dynamical Systems, Optimization, Scientific Computing, Complex Systems, and Network Science. Faculty are expected to engage in high-quality research, pursue competitive external funding, supervise students, and contribute to curriculum development and university service. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. Research Profile We are particularly interested in candidates working in one or more of the following areas: Partial and ordinary differential equations: analytical and computational methods for differential equations and mathematical modeling. Numerical analysis and scientific computing: numerical methods, computational linear algebra, high-performance scientific computing, tensor methods, and scalable algorithms. Optimization: continuous and discrete optimization, computational optimization, inverse problems, and optimization methods for scientific and engineering applications. Dynamical and complex systems: nonlinear dynamics, mathematical physics, network science, multiscale systems, and modeling of complex phenomena. Computational modeling and simulation: reduced-order modeling, simulation, data assimilation, digital twins, and computational methods for physical and engineering systems. Applications may include engineering, physics, energy systems, climate and environmental science, life sciences, neuroscience, sustainability, or other domains where mathematical and computational modeling plays a central role. Impact Xcelerator Collaboration We value candidates with the capacity to collaborate in applied research projects led by the Impact Xcelerator at IE School of Science and Technology, specifically in AI for Scientific Discovery, Advanced Simulation for Energy & Sustainability, Robotics & Autonomous Systems, and Health & MedTech Applications. The ability to contribute to multidisciplinary research initiatives that integrate computational modeling and applied physics expertise to address global challenges will be key to the role’s success. Key Responsibilities: Develop and teach courses at undergraduate and graduate levels in Computational Modeling and Applied Physics, including Numerical Methods, Differential Equations, Complex Systems, Dynamical Systems, Network theory and Applied Physics. Conduct high-impact research in areas such as multi-physics simulations, nonlinear dynamics, scientific computing, HPC, control theory, physics-informed neural networks, and computational/experimental modeling of physical systems, while actively securing competitive research funds. Supervise and mentor students across undergraduate, graduate, and Ph.D. programs. Collaborate with industry and research partners on innovative projects in robotics, sustainable energy, climate dynamics, and biomedical systems. Play an active role in curriculum development, incorporating emerging trends such as AI for scientific discovery, uncertainty quantification, and advanced simulation technologies. Participate in academic service and contribute to the strategic growth of the School of Science and Technology. We offer: A competitive salary in line with top-ranked European academic institutions. A generous seed research fund to cover travel, equipment and relocation costs. State-of-the-art campus facilities and support to build your lab infrastructure. A professional and stimulating international working environment with English as the de facto language. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme, plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Diversity in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment. Inspiring campus life on a conveniently located, state-of-the-art, unique campus in the hearts of Madrid and Segovia. About IE University and the School of Science and Technology IE University is an internationally recognized institution originally founded as a business school. We consider ourselves the most international institution of higher education with approximately 85% of our students coming from outside Spain and typically over 120 countries represented on campus. Our Madrid postgraduate campus is situated in the financial district of this vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of over 5 million people. In 2021 we opened the IE Tower –standing as one of the 5 towers in the business district of Madrid with a 6000-student capacity. The School of Science and Technology prepares students with industry relevant skills in the context of STEM and related educational programs. The school offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Applied Mathematics and Data analytics. For further information on the current faculty and lines of research, please visit IE Research Datalab The IE Impact Xcelerator offers new faculty the opportunity to participate in applied research labs in collaboration with research groups and companies in fields like healthcare, environmental science, finance, and cybersecurity, profiting from the rich network of IE Business School. PhD in Applied Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, Computational Science, Physics, Engineering  or relevant field by the appointment date, or a closely related area. Postdoctoral research experience is desirable but not required. Evidence of excellent research potential or achievement, including recent high-quality publications. Potential to attract competitive external funding. Commitment to excellent teaching, student supervision, and inclusive mentorship. Ability to contribute to interdisciplinary science and technology programs. Prior teaching experience and evidence of academic or professional contributions in the field will be viewed favorably. Create your dossier at Interfolio by Novem ber 1st and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/192573 Applications received before November 1st, 2026 will receive full consideration. The position will remain open until it is filled. Application Materials Cover letter. Curriculum vitae, including recent publications, funding record, teaching experience and supervision record. Research statement, including main achievements and future research plans for the next five years. Teaching statement. Evidence of teaching quality, if available. Up to three representative publications. Shortlisted candidates invited to an online interview may be asked to provide two to three confidential recommendation letters at a later stage. Pre-submission inquiries about the open positions may be addressed to Prof. Dae-Jin Lee Dae-Jin.Lee@ie.edu For questions about your dossier , go to: Interfolio Dossier Help"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192898": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Faculty Position in Materials Science 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia The IE School of Science and Technology at IE University invites applications for a full-time, open-rank faculty position in Material Science. The position may be offered at the tenure-track or tenured level, depending on the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research addresses one or more of the following areas: Smart, responsive, and multifunctional materials Composite materials, polymers, ceramics, metals, and alloys Nanomaterials and nanotechnology Biomaterials and materials for healthcare applications Materials for energy generation, conversion, and storage Sustainable materials, circular economy, and materials recycling Materials processing and advanced manufacturing Additive manufacturing and digital fabrication Computational materials science, materials modeling, and simulation Artificial intelligence and data-driven materials discovery Materials characterization, testing, performance, and failure analysis Candidates working at the intersection of these areas or applying multidisciplinary approaches to emerging challenges in energy, manufacturing, healthcare, and sustainability are strongly encouraged to apply. We also value candidates with the capacity to collaborate in applied research projects led by the IEX Labs at IE School of Science and Technology, particularly in areas related to renewable energy, advanced manufacturing, environmental systems, and intelligent infrastructure. The ability to contribute to multidisciplinary research initiatives that apply materials science expertise to develop sustainable, high-performance, intelligent, and resilient products and industrial systems will be key to the role’s success. Key Responsibilities: Develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Materials Science and Engineering, including courses such as  Materials Science, Resistance of Materials, Manufacturing Processes, and Sustainable Materials Establish and maintain a high-impact research program in materials science and engineering or a closely related area Publish research in high-quality international journals Pursue and secure competitive national and international research funding Supervise and mentor undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students Collaborate with academic researchers, industry partners, and public institutions Contribute to the development of the engineering curricula and academic programs Participate in academic service and support the strategic growth of the IE School of Science and Technology We offer: A competitive salary in line with top-ranked European academic institutions. A competitive research start-up package, providing seed funding for relocation, travel, and essential resources to launch research activities at IE University. State-of-the-art campus facilities and support to build your lab infrastructure. A professional and stimulating international working environment with English as the de facto language. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Diversity in an open-minded, inclusive and family-friendly environment. Inspiring campus life on a conveniently located, state-of-the-art unique campus in the hearts of Madrid and Segovia. About IE University and the School of Science and Technology IE University is an internationally recognized institution originally founded as a business school. We consider ourselves the most international institution of higher education with approximately 85% of our students coming from outside Spain and typically over 120 countries represented on campus. Our Madrid postgraduate campus is situated in the financial district of this vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of over 5 million people. In 2021 we opened the IE Tower –standing as one of the 5 towers in the business district of Madrid with a 6000-student capacity. The School of Science and Technology prepares students with industry relevant skills in the context of STEM and related educational programs. The school offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Applied Mathematics and Data analytics. For further information on the current faculty and lines of research, please visit the IE Research Datalab . The IEX Labs offer new faculty the opportunity to participate in applied research labs in collaboration with research groups and companies in fields like healthcare, environmental science, finance and cybersecurity, profiting from the rich network of IE Business School. We welcome applications from outstanding early-career researchers, including new PhD graduates and doctoral candidates who expect to complete their PhD before starting date, as well as established scholars with a strong record of high-quality research, academic publications, and competitive research funding. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in areas such as Materials Science, Resistance of Materials, Manufacturing Processes, and Sustainable Materials. They will also be expected to develop an internationally recognized research program and secure funding through competitive national and international research programs. Please provide the following: A cover letter describing their interest and fit to the position. A curriculum vitae, including a complete list of publications. A research statement outlining past achievements and future research plans. Evidence of teaching effectiveness, where available. Contact information of three potential references that we may contact for a reference letter. For consideration create your dossier and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/192898 Applications received before November 1st, 2026, will receive full consideration . The search will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192903": {
