      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia The IE School of Science and Technology at IE University invites applications for a full-time, open-rank faculty position in Mechanical Engineering, with a specialization in Fluid Mechanics. The position may be offered at the tenure-track or tenured level, depending on the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research addresses one or more of the following areas: Theoretical, experimental, and computational fluid mechanics Computational fluid dynamics and high-performance computing Aerodynamics and aerospace applications Thermal-fluid systems, heat transfer, and energy conversion Renewable energy systems, including wind, hydro, and ocean energy Fluid mechanics for sustainable buildings, cities, and transportation Biofluid mechanics and biomedical applications Candidates working at the intersection of these areas or applying multidisciplinary approaches to emerging challenges in energy, manufacturing, healthcare, and sustainability are strongly encouraged to apply. We also value candidates with the capacity to collaborate in applied research projects led by the IEX Labs at IE School of Science and Technology, particularly in areas related to renewable energy, advanced manufacturing, environmental systems, and intelligent infrastructure. The ability to contribute to multidisciplinary research initiatives that apply fluid mechanics expertise to develop efficient, sustainable, intelligent, and resilient engineering systems will be key to the role’s success. Key Responsibilities: Develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Mechanical Engineering, including courses such as Fluid Mechanics, Thermodynamics, Heat Transfer, Computational Fluid 