    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192904": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Faculty Position in Industrial Engineering (Manufacturing Systems) 2027-2028",
      "description": "Posted: Sep 04, 2026 Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia The IE School of Science and Technology at IE University invites applications for a full-time, open-rank faculty position in Industrial Engineering, with a specialization in Manufacturing Systems and Engineering. The position may be offered at the tenure-track or tenured level, depending on the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research addresses one or more of the following areas: Advanced manufacturing systems and technologies Warehousing, Smart manufacturing, Industry X.0 Digital manufacturing, digital twins, and cyber-physical production systems Manufacturing processes, process modeling, monitoring, and optimization Robotics, industrial automation, and human–robot collaboration Computer-aided design, manufacturing, and engineering Production systems design, planning, scheduling, and control Artificial intelligence, machine learning, and data analytics for manufacturing Sustainable manufacturing, circular production systems, and industrial decarbonization Quality engineering, reliability, maintenance, and industrial asset management Human-centered manufacturing, ergonomics, and the future of work Candidates working at the intersection of these areas or applying multidisciplinary approaches to emerging challenges in manufacturing, automation, digitalization, and sustainability are strongly encouraged to apply. We also value candidates with the capacity to collaborate in applied research projects led by the IEX Labs at IE School of Science and Technology, particularly in areas of advanced manufacturing, industrial automation, robotics, digital twins, and sustainable production systems. The ability to contribute to multidisciplinary research initiatives that apply industrial engineering expertise to build intelligent, efficient, resilient, and sustainable manufacturing systems will be key to the role’s success. Key Responsibilities: Develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Industrial Engineering, including courses such as Manufacturing Systems, Manufacturing Processes, Production Systems, Industrial Automation, and Computer-Aided Design and Manufacturing Establish and maintain a high-impact research program in manufacturing systems and engineering or a closely related area Publish research in high-quality international journals Pursue and secure competitive national and international research funding Supervise and mentor undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students Collaborate with academic researchers, industry partners, and public institutions Contribute to the development of the engineering curricula and academic programs Participate in academic service and support the strategic growth of the IE School of Science and Technology We offer: A competitive salary in line with top-ranked European academic institutions. A competitive research start-up package, providing seed funding for relocation, travel, and essential resources to launch research activities at IE University. State-of-the-art campus facilities and support to build your lab infrastructure. A professional and stimulating international working environment with English as the de facto language. Full access to public health services through membership of the National Insurance Scheme plus a discount plan to acquire an additional private health insurance plan. Diversity in an open-minded, inclusive and family-friendly environment. Inspiring campus life on a conveniently located, state-of-the-art unique campus in the hearts of Madrid and Segovia. About IE University and the School of Science and Technology IE University is an internationally recognized institution originally founded as a business school. We consider ourselves the most international institution of higher education with approximately 85% of our students coming from outside Spain and typically over 120 countries represented on campus. Our Madrid postgraduate campus is situated in the financial district of this vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of over 5 million people. In 2021 we opened the IE Tower –standing as one of the 5 towers in the business district of Madrid with a 6000-student capacity. The School of Science and Technology prepares students with industry relevant skills in the context of STEM and related educational programs. The school offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Applied Mathematics and Data analytics. For further information on the current faculty and lines of research, please visit the IE Research Datalab . The IEX Labs offer new faculty the opportunity to participate in applied research labs in collaboration with research groups and companies in fields like healthcare, environmental science, finance and cybersecurity, profiting from the rich network of IE Business School. We welcome applications from outstanding early-career researchers, including new PhD graduates and doctoral candidates who expect to complete their PhD before the appointment begins, as well as established scholars with a strong record of high-quality research, academic publications, and competitive research funding. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in areas such as Manufacturing Processes and Systems, Production Systems, Industrial Instrumentation for Automation, and Cyber-physical systems and digital manufacturing. They will also be expected to develop an internationally recognized research program and secure funding through competitive national and international research programs. Please provide the following: A cover letter describing their interest and fit to the position. A curriculum vitae, including a complete list of publications. A research statement outlining past achievements and future research plans. Evidence of teaching effectiveness, where available. Contact information of three potential references that we may contact for a reference letter. For consideration create your dossier and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/192904 Applications received before November 1st, 2026, will receive full consideration . The search will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192907": {
