      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia The IE School of Science and Technology at IE University invites applications for a full-time, open-rank faculty position in Electrical Engineering with a specialization in Power and Energy Systems. The position may be offered at the tenure-track or tenured level, depending on the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research addresses one or more of the following areas: Power and energy systems engineering, planning, operation, and optimization Electricity markets, pricing mechanisms, and power-system modeling Smart grids, microgrids, and distributed energy resources Renewable energy systems Energy harvesting, conversion, and storage Electric machines, motors, and drives Power electronics, electrical apparatus, protection, and control Digitalization, resilience, cybersecurity, and artificial intelligence in energy systems Candidates working at the intersection of these areas or applying multidisciplinary approaches to emerging energy challenges are strongly encouraged to apply. We value candidates with the capacity to collaborate in applied research projects led by the IEX Labs at IE School of Science and Technology, particularly in area of Smart Grids and Renewable Energy. The ability to contribute to multidisciplinary research initiatives that apply electrical engineering expertise to build sustainable, intelligent, and secure systems will be key to the role’s success. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. Key Responsibilities: Develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Electrical Engineering, including courses such as Electric Circuits, Energy Economics, Energy Systems, and Electric Power Generation and Distribution Establish and maintain a high-impact research progr