    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193080": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Environmental Technology 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Science and Technology Location: Madrid and Segovia IE University´s , School of Science and Technology invites applications for full-time tenure-track faculty positions in Environmental Technology. The successful candidates will join an interdisciplinary environmental science and technology area connected to the BSc in Environmental Sciences for Sustainability and to the broader research ecosystem of the School. The appointment starts in the academic year 2027-2028. We seek outstanding junior or early mid-career scholars with a strong research trajectory, clear potential for international visibility, and the capacity to build externally funded research programs while contributing to high-quality teaching and student mentorship. Candidates should be able to work across disciplinary boundaries and translate environmental science into technological, analytical, or decision-support solutions. Priority Areas The search is intentionally broad within the following priority areas: Environmental and Bioprocess Engineering: Transport phenomena, separations, reactor design, physical and reactive transport, process intensification, pilot-scale environmental or bioprocess systems, and resource recovery. Ecohydrology, Hydrogeology and Water Management: Groundwater and catchment hydrology, contaminant transport, water reuse, drought and flood risk, soil-water-plant processes, monitoring, and process-based or spatial modelling. Experimental Environmental Synthetic Biology and Metabolic Engineering: Experimental design-build-test-learn approaches for engineered strains or microbial consortia applied to pollutant transformation, C1/CO2 conversion, waste-to-value processes, resource recovery, and environmental bioprocess scale-up. Environmental Bioinformatics and Computational Biology: Emphasis on environmental and microbial genomics, including genome-resolved metagenomics, comparative and functional genomics, omics integration, protein or enzyme modelling, reproducible pipelines, FAIR data practices, and environmental technology applications. Exceptional candidates in other areas of environmental technology will also be considered where they bring a strong quantitative, engineering or technology-development profile that clearly complements the School’s existing strengths and teaching needs. Key Responsibilities Teach at undergraduate and graduate levels in English in Environmental Sciences for Sustainability and related programs. Develop a high-impact, externally funded research agenda in one or more of the priority areas above. Publish in high-quality peer-reviewed venues and build international research collaborations. Supervise and mentor undergraduate, graduate and doctoral students. Contribute to curriculum development, including laboratory, computational, field, and/or project-based learning where relevant. Collaborate with academic, public-sector, NGO and industry partners on applied environmental challenges. Participate in academic service and contribute to the strategic growth of the School of Science and Technology. We Offer A competitive salary in line with leading European academic institutions. A seed research fund to support travel, equipment, relocation and initial research activity. Access to teaching and research facilities, including environmental technology, earth and life sciences, chemistry, and molecular biology laboratory infrastructure. A professional and international working environment with English as the working language. Access to public health services through the Spanish National Insurance Scheme, plus the option of additional private health insurance. An open-minded, inclusive and family-friendly environment. Campus life across Madrid and Segovia, including the historic Segovia campus and IE Tower in Madrid. About IE University and the School of Science and Technology IE University is an internationally recognized institution originally founded as a business school. The university has a highly international student body and campuses in Madrid and Segovia. The School of Science and Technology offers undergraduate and graduate programs in areas including Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Applied Mathematics, Data Analytics and Environmental Science. The Environmental Sciences for Sustainability program is connected to teaching and research facilities in Segovia and Madrid, including laboratories for environmental technology, chemistry, molecular biology, earth and life sciences, and data-driven science. New faculty are expected to contribute to the development of an ambitious, interdisciplinary environmental science and technology area with strong links to applied research and external partners. For further information about the School, please visit the IE School of Science and Technology website . PhD in a relevant field by the appointment date, including engineering (e.g., chemical, civil, or environmental), environmental science, computational biology, or related areas. Evidence of excellent research potential or achievement, including recent high-quality publications. Potential to attract competitive external funding. Commitment to excellent teaching, student supervision, and inclusive mentorship. Ability to contribute to interdisciplinary environmental science and technology programs. Spanish language skills are not required. Our working language is English. Both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. Please submit the following materials: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae, including recent publications, funding record, teaching experience and supervision record. Research statement, including main achievements and future research plans for the next five years. Teaching statement. Evidence of teaching quality, if available. Up to three representative publications. Shortlisted candidates invited to an online interview may be asked to provide two to three confidential recommendation letters at a later stage. For consideration create your dossier and apply at: https://apply.interfolio.com/193080 Applications received before November 1st, 2026 , will receive full consideration. The search will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195869": {
      "title": "Arts and Humanities Open Rank Position 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: School of Arts & Humanities Location: Madrid & Segovia, Spain Posted: Oct 19, 2026 Deadline: Nov 30, 2026 The School of Arts and Humanities at IE University invites applications for an open-rank position (assistant or associate professor) in Digital Humanities, effective September 2027. We are looking for candidates with a PhD in a humanistic discipline who employ computational methods in their research. This may include, but is not limited to data visualization, digital reconstruction, network analysis, NLP, text mining, and corpora development. Candidates should be firmly committed to scholarship in one of the disciplines within the humanities. While not required, a focus on one or more regions in the Global South, the premodern period, and/or the ability to contribute to the School’s UNESCO Chair in AI Ethics will also be considered a strong asset for this role. Candidates should have the ability to publish in top-tier peer-reviewed journals, to teach courses related to their expertise, and to interact and work closely with faculty from other disciplines. Teaching responsibilities are approximately a 2-1 load, divided across introductory and advanced undergraduate students, as well as master-level programs in other schools. English is our working language and the primary language of instruction. Knowledge of Spanish is therefore not required. IE University, which grew out of IE Business School, has taken a leading position in Europe among institutions of higher education for its excellence in innovation and learning technologies. In addition to the Business School, we have schools of Law, Politics, Economics and Global Affairs, Architecture and Design, Arts & Humanities, and the school of Science & Technology. IE’s programs are highly ranked and recognized in the international press. IE’s diverse faculty comes from around the world, and is encouraged to develop excellence in research, teaching, and leadership within their areas of expertise. IE University has campuses in Madrid and Segovia, Spain. Madrid is a vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of 5+ million that offers an enormous range of professional and leisure opportunities. Segovia is a beautiful World-Heritage city that offers the pleasures of a small city environment, the possibility of many outdoor activities, and easy access (30 minutes by bullet train) to the heart of bustling Madrid. Please visit: http://www.ie.edu/university/home/ to learn more about IE University. A PhD in a humanistic discipline who employ computational methods in their research. Applications should include a cover letter and CV, a one-page teaching statement, three confidential recommendation letters, and one sample research paper. We will be holding virtual interviews in January 2027. Interested candidates should submit their application before November 30, 2026 via Interfolio at: https://apply.interfolio.com/195869 For help with your application and your dossier, contact Intefolio Help. https://product-help.interfolio.com/en_US/dossier or help@interfolio.com Address substantive questions to the Area Director of the School of Arts and Humanities, Professor Shana Cooperstein shana.cooperstein@ie.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196200": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Position(s) in Communication and Media 2027-2028",
      "description": "Department: IE University: Business School: Communication and Media Location: Madrid & Segovia, Spain Posted: Oct 22, 2026 Deadline: Nov 23, 2026 IE University invites qualified candidates in communication to apply for a tenure-track position. The positions are at the Assistant or Experienced Assistant Professor level in the Communication and Media Department, beginning in September 2027. We particularly welcome applications from candidates with expertise in Political Communication and/or Environmental Communication. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, misinformation and disinformation, public opinion, news and media trust, civic engagement, climate change communication, and sustainability communication. We also welcome applied or solutions-oriented research that connects theoretical insights to areas of practice such as journalism, strategic communication, public policy, advocacy, or platform and technology governance. Candidates using any methodological approach are welcome to apply, with preference for those with expertise in quantitative, computational and/or experimental methods. The selected candidate(s) will join and complement a vibrant and growing community of researchers in Communication and Media whose work encompasses areas as diverse as journalism studies, critical-cultural approaches, digital media studies, cultural production, film and media, globalization, public affairs, corporate ethics, and consumer behavior. English is the working language of our diverse, international faculty and student community. Knowledge of Spanish is not required. The successful candidates will hold a Ph.D. in Communication or a related discipline. Prior teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level is desirable but not required. Our faculty are expected to present their work in international venues and to publish in peer-reviewed journals. Teaching requirements for these positions are the standard for research-active institutions. The successful candidate will teach and advise students in the portfolio of bachelor and master programs of the Business School. New faculty members are expected to provide intellectual leadership within IE University in their areas of expertise, and to contribute to a collegial atmosphere and a diverse, inclusive campus life. IE University is an internationally recognized institution comprising IE Business School, IE School of Politics, Economics and Global Affairs, IE School of Science & Technology, IE Law School, IE School of Architecture and Design, and the IE School of Humanities. We are among the most international institutions of higher education with approximately 85% of our students coming from outside Spain and typically over 120 countries represented on campus. Our Madrid campus is situated in the financial district of this vibrant, cosmopolitan capital city of over 5 million people. In 2021, we opened the doors to the IE Learning Tower – a vertical undergraduate campus located on the northern edge of Madrid’s city center. Our Segovia campus is located in the historic quarter of this World-Heritage city, 30 minutes by high-speed train from Madrid. The successful candidates will hold a Ph.D. in Communication or a related discipline. Prior teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level is desirable but not required. Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, three confidential recommendation letters, research and teaching statements, and evidence of teaching effectiveness, if applicable. Please submit your application by November 23, 2026 via Interfol io at: https://apply.interfolio.com/196200 Specific enquiries about the Department or the position can be made to Prof. Vincent Doyle at vdoyle@faculty.ie.edu"
    }
  },
